{{also|KAON|kaón|käön}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From contracted pronunciation of ''K-[[meson]]''

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkeɪˌɑn/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|particle}} any of four [[unstable]] [[subatomic particle]]s, [[meson]]s, they are a [[combination]] of a [[strange]] [[quark]] or [[antiquark]] and either an [[up]] or [[down]] quark or antiquark
#* K<sup>0</sup>: strange quark + down antiquark
#* K<sup>0*</sup> ([[antiparticle]] of K<sup>0</sup>): down quark + strange antiquark
#* K<sup>+</sup>: strange quark + up antiquark
#* K<sup>-</sup> ([[antiparticle]] of K<sup>+</sup>): up quark + strange antiquark

